The fix adds a check to ensure that `zdev->zbus->bus` is not NULL before attempting to dereference it. If it is NULL, the function exits early, preventing the dereference of a NULL pointer and thus avoiding a crash. The comment clarifies that the scanning of the PCI function will occur once function 0 is available, aligning the behavior with expected outcomes.

